# Add `userDefinedContext` to validation context · Issue #843 · arktypeio/arktype
created: 2023-08-18, last updated: 2026-04-17, [Read more](https://github.com/arktypeio/arktype/issues/843)

Add `userDefinedContext` (along with `objectPath` and existing `root` and `path`) to validation context
and `userDefinedContext` to define it
...
Make context to have a variable that user can define in narrow-like function before validation,
which gets removed after exiting from the tree node it was added in
```
const S = scope({
stringWithInheritedMaxLength: narrow(
'string',
(data, context) => data.length <= context.userDefinedContext.maxStringLength,
),
});
const UserA = S
.withContext((data) => { return {maxStringLength: data.max} })
.type({
max: 'integer>0',
name: 'stringWithInheritedMaxLength',
friends: `stringWithInheritedMaxLength[]`,
})
const UserB = S.type({
max: 'integer>0',
name: 'stringWithInheritedMaxLength',
...
}, {
...
})
...
})
```
This context also can be passed into the validator itself, if user needs that
```
UserLike({name: 'foo', friends: ['bar']}, {userDefinedContext: {maxStringLength: 123}})
```

